## Modules
`common.py` constants (k grid, ranks, seed), matrix loading, group/temporal/strength splits. `fa.py` probabilistic factor analysis with
missing data (EM, noise floor 1e-2), posterior for a new row, closed-form design risk (T1). `select_rules.py` selection rules S0–S7
(S6 greedy Bayesian V-optimal design with Sherman–Morrison gains; S3 wrapper and S6u checked against brute force). `infer_rules.py`,
`baselines.py` inference rules P0–P6. `state.py`, `state2.py` per-fold fits. `mteb_cells.py` cell/revision/organisation rules.

## Definitions the result files rely on
* Score = MTEB `main_score` x 100 ("raw points"); errors are RMSE in raw points unless the column says `_std` (standardised per training benchmark).
* **Primary score (common target set, `ct_*` files):** 50 fixed random splits of the 328 benchmarks into a candidate pool C and a target set T (|T| = 109, stratified by task type, never selectable).
  A held-out model reveals k benchmarks chosen among its observed C cells; every rule is scored on the model's observed T cells (RMSE, raw points), per split, then averaged over the model's
  eligible splits (>= k observed C and >= 37 observed T cells; a model enters k if eligible in >= 20 splits). The floor is the same model's error on the same T with all its observed C cells revealed.
  `subset = fixed`: models that enter at k_max = 109 (the same models at every k).  `results/COLUMNS.md` lists each column and the function that computes it.
* **Secondary score (`*_rms.csv`):** targets are the model's remaining observed cells R_m \ S (they change with k); models with run set <= k are excluded and counted (`n_excluded_at_k`).
* Held-out units are organisation groups (10 folds over 83 groups); everything (standardisation, factor fit, rank, margins) is fitted on training models
  only. `T`: train on the 70% earliest releases, test on later ones; `S`: train on the 75% weakest by additive offset, test on the strongest 25%.
* Floor = the model's own error when all other benchmarks of its run set are revealed (leave-one-benchmark-out).
* Curve CI: group bootstrap (resample held-out groups, B=5000), mean over models with equal weight per model. `gain_mean` = RMSE(S0) - RMSE(S6) (positive: S6 better).
* `k_emp = 9999` means the threshold was not reached on the grid.
